<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>I take Him at His word indeed:</l><l>“Christ died for sinners”—this I read;</l><l>For in my heart I find a need</l><l>Of Him to be my Savior!</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>That He should leave His place on high</l><l>And come for sinful man to die,</l><l>You count it strange? So once did I</l><l>Before I knew my Savior!</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>And, oh, that He fulfilled may see</l><l>The travail of His soul in me,</l><l>And with His work contented be,</l><l>As I with my dear Savior!</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Yes, living, dying, let me bring</l><l>My strength, my solace from this spring—</l><l>That He who lives to be my King</l><l>Once died to be my Savior!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
